            <div xml:id="d1098">

                <pb facs="1072" n="906" xml:id="pg906"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/20395</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of War to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">War Department</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-01-17">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 17, 1917</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Secretary of War presents his compliments to the Honorable the Secretary of
                    State, and has the honor to inclose, herewith, for his information, copy of a
                    letter from the commanding general, Southern Department, Fort Sam Houston,
                    Texas, dated January 10, 1917, quoting a report made by the Department
                    intelligence officer, relative to the present status and activities in the plan
                    of San Diego.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Newton D. Baker</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d1098-a1.xml" xpointer="d1098-a1"/>
